WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.710
&gt;&gt;&gt; This morning CNN's Christiane Amanpour
just had an exclusive one-on-one sitdown with

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.430
former president Barack Obama.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:11.040
They are in Athens, Greece, the birthplace
of democracy, and had a candid discussion

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.890
about the war on Ukraine, the upcoming U.S.
Election and how to navigate a global tricky

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.910
relationship with autocratic leaders.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.800
She will join us in a moment.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.270
First, here is part of that conversation.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:29.920
&gt;&gt; Reporter: President Biden, a man you know
extremely well, has made the defense of democracy

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.090
the sort of centerpiece of his administration.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:37.820
It just so happens that right now there is
also not just, you know, threats to democracy

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.510
by dictatorships and autocrats, but liberal
democracy as well.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:47.420
He has called the president of China dictator
and they are sticking with it.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:55.289
He also hosted the prime minister of India,
Modi, who is considered autocratic, or at

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:56.289
[8:13:54 AM]

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.700
considered autocratic, or at least a liberal
Democrat.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.680
What is the point, I guess, or how should
a president engage with those kinds of leaders

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.290
either in the naming of them or the dealing
with them?

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.480
&gt;&gt; Look, it's complicated.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:16.860
The president of the united States has a lot
of equities, and when I was president I would

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:26.299
deal with figures and in some cases who were
allies who, you know, if you press me in private,

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:36.390
do they run their governments and their political
parties in ways that I would say are ideally

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.390
democratic?

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.390
I would have to say no.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.390
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Do you want to name names?

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.550
&gt;&gt; Of course not.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.290
But you had to do business with them because
they are important for national security reasons.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:51.490
You know, there are a range of economic interests.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:55.250
I dealt with China to get the Paris accords
done.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.250
[8:14:55 AM]

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.250
Paris accords done.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.909
I dealt with Modi to get the Paris accords
done because you think climate change is something

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:06.860
that transcends any particular momentary issues.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.759
It's a problem that humanity has to deal with
over the next several decades in a serious

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:12.540
way.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:18.160
I do think that it is appropriate for the
president of the United States where he or

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:28.280
she can to uphold those principles and to
challenge whether behind closed doors or in

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.989
public trends that are troubling.

00:02:31.989 --> 00:02:39.790
And so I am less concerned about labels than
I am concerned about specific practices.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:45.540
I think it is important for the president
of the United States to say that if you have

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:55.611
uighurs in China who are being placed in mass
camps and reeducated, quote, unquote, that's

00:02:55.611 --> 00:02:56.611
a problem.

00:02:56.611 --> 00:02:57.611
[8:15:56 AM]

00:02:57.611 --> 00:02:58.611
problem.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:00.810
That's a challenge to all of us, and we have
to pay attention to it.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:09.409
I think it is true that if the president meets
with prime minister Modi, then the protection

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:17.140
of the Muslim minority in a majority hindu
India, that's something worth mentioning because

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:23.020
-- and by the way, if I had a conversation
with prime minister Modi, who I know well,

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:31.550
part of my argument would be that if you do
not protect the rights of ethnic minorities

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:39.480
in India, then there is a strong possibility
India at some point starts pulling apart and

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:46.610
we've seen what happens when you start getting
those kinds of large internal conflicts.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:51.760
So that would be contrary to the interests,
not just a Muslim India, but also hindu India.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:56.090
So I think it's important to be able to talk
about these things honestly.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.090
[8:16:57 AM]

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.090
honestly.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.959
You are never going to have -- things are
never going to be as clean as you'd like because

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:04.320
the world is complicated.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:09.140
They will /* she will join us later tonight.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.189
&gt;&gt; 10:00 P.M.

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:16.320
Eastern you see right there.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.320
Tune in for that.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.700
Right now we want to bring in CNN political
analyst, senior political correspondent at

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.430
"The New York Times" Maggie Haberman.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:27.110
I want to talk about everything that you are
deeply engaged in covering every single day

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:33.010
but listening to that the former president
has been more candid since he left office.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:38.440
Digging in on a central issue to the current
president but also I think to some degree

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.440
the campaign coming up.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.400
&gt;&gt; I think the campaign coming up I think
he was talking primarily about relations with

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.400
foreign leaders.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:48.000
Realistically, it can apply domestically,
too.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.949
This is an argument that actually you haven't
seen very many Democrats make about the pro-democracy

00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:59.140
efforts which is that it's complicated, that
it's not clean cut, it's not, you know, up

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:00.140
and down always.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.140
[8:17:59 AM]

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.140
know, up and down always.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:04.199
Sometimes you have to make decisions that
are not necessarily in keeping with other

00:05:04.199 --> 00:05:07.190
professed ideals but because there is a broader
world out there.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:14.150
I wonder how much we will see president Obama
out there making arguments like this that

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:17.150
supplement what president Biden has been saying.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:21.300
I mean, I think that there is always one of
the concerns that Democrats have, particularly

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:25.000
people around Joe Biden have, is that Obama
is such a better communicator, such a more

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.580
natural communicator that is there going to
be that comparison with Obama.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.880
I think speaks to the moment we are in and
the moment the Democrats find themselves in,

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:34.880
you know.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.310
I don't know how much of this Obama is discussing
with the white house.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:41.020
I don't know how much of this is just him
wanting to make his voice heard.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.360
But I do wonder if it portends hearing from
him more going forward.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.730
&gt;&gt; It's also just really interesting timing
that he is doing this right after as Christiane

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:56.699
pointed out Biden at that fundraiser in San
Francisco called XI a dictator and the fact

00:05:56.699 --> 00:05:57.979
he is hosting Modi.

00:05:57.979 --> 00:05:58.979
The white house did get some

00:05:58.979 --> 00:05:59.979
[8:19:00 AM]

00:05:59.979 --> 00:06:02.319
The white house did get some concessions,
they are going to hold a joint press conference.

00:06:02.319 --> 00:06:03.360
That's a big deal.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.810
Modi didn't want to do that.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.789
Journalists can ask him these hard question,
too.

00:06:09.789 --> 00:06:13.849
Do you think we will hear from the white house
whether or not president Biden brought up

00:06:13.849 --> 00:06:16.310
these many human rights concerns?

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:18.510
Treatment of journalists in India?

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.260
&gt;&gt; I think that's something that the white
house will address.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:24.740
I think they tend to be willing to engage
on issues like that.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.840
I think whether they are going to want to
have a broader conversation about the contradiction

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:33.979
between clearly outlining XI --
&gt;&gt; In the same week.

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:37.650
&gt;&gt; In the same week, when you are hosting
Modi in person.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:42.400
So I do think this is going to be a contradiction
they are going to get pushed on.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.491
Again I think the point that Obama is making
is that when you speak in absolutes, you are

00:06:46.491 --> 00:06:52.270
going to get questions like that even if your
commitment is absolute to democracy and to

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:55.919
democracies globally that we are living in
a complicated world.

00:06:55.919 --> 00:06:57.430
&gt;&gt; Stick with us.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.440
We have Christiane Amanpour with us now.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.440
After that interview, we just

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.440
[8:20:01 AM]

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:06.090
After that interview, we just heard a block
of that interview and we were talking with

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.710
Maggie about the dynamic and how candid the
former president was.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:14.800
&gt;&gt; Was your sense of things after talking
to him?

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.180
&gt;&gt; Well, look, you know, this is the question,
right?

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:23.180
President Biden has made defending democracy
the centerpiece of his administration.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.180
Look at Ukraine.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.310
Obviously, the defense of democratic Ukraine.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.650
But as they say, you know, it's complicated.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.099
There is real politic.

00:07:30.099 --> 00:07:35.770
You can go back to Kissinger for that kind
of foreign policy of trying to maintain stability.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:41.070
What you are seeing and you probably discussed
this many Democrats don't like this.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:46.419
They see that Modi is autocratic, that Modi
is cracking down on the press, on religious

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:51.680
minorities, the Muslim minorities on political
opposition and that is autocratic or at the

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.350
least a liberal democracy.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:08:01.199
As you know, there is a very, very keen desire
to try to win Modi over to try to help him

00:08:01.199 --> 00:08:02.289
peel away from China.

00:08:02.289 --> 00:08:03.289
[8:21:02 AM]

00:08:03.289 --> 00:08:04.289
peel away from China.

00:08:04.289 --> 00:08:08.180
The entire focus, it looks like at the moment,
of America's foreign policy is on China.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:12.880
And, therefore, they are trying to get as
much support as they can, including they are

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:19.350
trying to get India's support to bolster the
not the confrontation, but the idea of trying

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.860
to make sure that China doesn't pose an even
more dangerous threat.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.680
It's risky, of course.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:29.900
Modi has not and India has not gone ahead
with many of the U.N. Resolutions he against

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:34.150
Russia on this Ukraine war, keeps buying Russian
oil.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.019
There is a lot to be discussed between them.

00:08:38.019 --> 00:08:40.400
&gt;&gt; This an exclusive interview.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:45.390
The fact that you got so much time with former
president Obama in this moment, I was saying

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:48.959
to Phil, you are the perfect person to interview
him in this moment.

00:08:48.959 --> 00:08:53.780
Can you give us a little bit of a highlight
of what people will see tonight?

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:54.780
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:09:00.410
Well, it is an amazing time to get this interview
because the former president is very, very,

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:05.660
very much engaged in the promotion of global
democracy

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:06.660
[8:22:04 AM]

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.910
promotion of global democracy and the strengthening
of American democracy.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:13.160
He is here as part of his foundation with
dozens if not more than 100 what we call global

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.670
youth leaders from his foundation, men and
women, young men and women they are trying

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:23.230
to help really connect together and build
and strengthen all of the aspects of democracy

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:27.200
from a grass roots up vision, if you like,
around world.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.829
Here we are in Athens, the birthplace of modern
democracy.

00:09:30.829 --> 00:09:34.459
So essentially we talked about the U.S. Democracy.

00:09:34.459 --> 00:09:40.230
We talked about what he called creaky institutions
around the world that need to be strengthened

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:41.240
even in the U.S.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:45.890
I asked him about the spectacle of a former
president who is being indicted on federal

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:50.930
charges actually running for office, the highest
office in the land, perhaps the world.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:57.680
He said it's not ideal, but it is absolutely
fundamental for Americans and others around

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:02.880
the world to see that America upholds the
rule of law and that the law applies to everybody.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:04.020
He said that was absolutely fundamental.

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.020
[8:23:05 AM]

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.020
fundamental.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.020
I will say another thing, too.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:13.530
He spoke at length about global and U.S. Inequality
and inequity, income inequality and all the

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:19.950
other inequalities that are so fundamental
to the degradation of democracy and around

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:20.950
the world.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:27.250
To be fair, and I'll just going to say it,
he said the submarine, the submersible sinking

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:32.820
and we don't quite know what's going to happen
is a terrible tragedy, and yet not enough,

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:40.320
you know, resources and attention was put
on 750 poor people who were caught in the

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:45.890
boat off the coast of Greece where we are
right now and who almost all have died except

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:49.279
for maybe over 100 people were saved.

00:10:49.279 --> 00:10:50.290
These are the kinds of

